      "text": "```\nNATURAL → MANUFACTURED FIBER TIMELINE\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  All textiles from       1892: Rayon       1938: Nylon           |\n|  plant/animal until      First man-made    First fully           |\n|  late 19th century       fiber (cellulose  synthetic fiber       |\n|                          source, chemical  (petrochem)           |\n|                          process)                                |\n|                                            1941: Polyester       |\n|                                            ICI Terylene          |\n|                                                                  |\n|                                            1958: Spandex/Lycra   |\n|                                            Du Pont — elastomeric |\n|                                                                  |\n|  TODAY: ~65% of global fiber consumption is synthetic            |\n|  Polyester alone: ~54% of all fiber produced                     |\n|  Cotton: ~24% (declining)                                        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
